# PR Template

- Always use `.github/pull_request_template.md`. Keep its section headings, order, checklist items, and prompts.
- Never check **I have tested these changes in-game**. That box is reserved for a human after Retail QA. Do not check it to make CI pass, even if automated tests passed or a previous PR checked it.
- You MAY check **In-game testing is not applicable to this change** only when there are no packaged addon/runtime changes, except explicitly safe TOC metadata or files proven not to ship (`SpectrumFederation/AGENTS.md` via zip `-x`). Do not infer harmlessness from extension. Images, sounds, fonts, libraries, localization, and unknown packaged files all require human QA.
- A TOC change may use N/A only when the inspected diff is limited to explicitly safe metadata (`## Version`, `## X-Wago-ID`, and the small informational `X-*` allowlist). Do not assume a TOC change is harmless.
- Unknown, unreadable, or runtime TOC fields (`## Interface`, dependencies, SavedVariables, LoadOnDemand, file-list/load-order, and anything not allowlisted) require human QA. Leave N/A unchecked and leave **tested in-game** unchecked for the human.
- If unsure whether a packaged file affects the addon, require human QA. Never check **tested in-game** on behalf of a human.
- Always check **WoW Client Type → Retail**. This addon targets Retail. Checking Retail is the product target, not a claim that in-game QA was done. Leave Classic, PTR, and Beta unchecked unless the change is specifically for those clients.
- In **Testing**, report automated and static validation actually run. If N/A is selected, say that in-game QA is not applicable and why. If the change needs Retail QA, state that it was not performed. You may optionally add suggested in-game test steps as unchecked checkboxes for the human; never mark those complete.
- Do not claim in-game verification, and do not fabricate screenshots or videos as Retail proof.
- Check **I have added/updated localization strings in `locale/enUS.lua` if applicable** only after auditing the PR diff against the Localization policy in `SpectrumFederation/AGENTS.md`: either the change added/updated locale keys for new/modified user-facing strings, or the diff introduced no new/modified user-facing addon strings. Do not check this box automatically, assume compliance, or edit `locale/enUS.lua` merely to satisfy the checkbox.
- For **I've linked this PR to any related issues**, follow root `AGENTS.md` (**Issue-backed PR Development linking**). Check it only after the formal GitHub Issue ↔ PR Development relationship exists for an owner-supplied or otherwise authoritative issue for the task. Leave it unchecked when that link was not created. Do not invent or check for unrelated issues. Linked-issue remains optional in CI.
- `.github/scripts/validate_pr_template.py` requires exactly one in-game testing state. N/A is rejected when packaged addon files changed, or when a TOC change is runtime-affecting, unknown, or not inspectable. Linked-issue remains optional in CI.
